From: Quectel (elijah.zhou) <elijah.zhou@quectel.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: spi-nor: xmc: add support for XMC XM25QH256C

The XMC XM25QH256C is a 32MB SPI NOR chip. As it is larger than 16MB it
requires 4-byte address opcodes. Added to support a secondary flash
supplier (Quectel SDM108A / MorseMicro HaLowLink APX).

Datasheet provided by Quectel. JEDEC ID 0x204019.

Signed-off-by: Lyall Beveridge <lyall.beveridge@morsemicro.com>
---
 drivers/mtd/spi-nor/xmc.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/mtd/spi-nor/xmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/spi-nor/xmc.c
@@ -22,6 +22,10 @@ static const struct flash_info xmc_nor_p
 	{ "XM25QH128C", INFO(0x204018, 0, 64 * 1024, 256)
 		NO_SFDP_FLAGS(SECT_4K | SPI_NOR_DUAL_READ |
 			      SPI_NOR_QUAD_READ) },
+	{ "XM25QH256C", INFO(0x204019, 0, 64 * 1024, 512)
+		FIXUP_FLAGS(SPI_NOR_4B_OPCODES)
+		NO_SFDP_FLAGS(SECT_4K | SPI_NOR_DUAL_READ |
+			      SPI_NOR_QUAD_READ) },
 };
 
 const struct spi_nor_manufacturer spi_nor_xmc = {
